# CivicSense environment configuration
#
# The app runs fully as a demo (in-memory data + deterministic AI engine)
# WITHOUT any of the variables below being set. Fill these in only when you
# want to connect a real Supabase project and/or a real AI/ML classification API.

# --- Supabase ---
# Create a project at https://supabase.com, then copy these from
# Project Settings -> API. Run supabase/schema.sql in the SQL editor first.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# --- Real email-OTP login (citizens) ---
# Works out of the box with Supabase's default email sending once
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL / VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY below are set — no extra code
# or secrets needed. Supabase Auth (GoTrue) generates, sends, and verifies
# the OTP itself via supabase.auth.signInWithOtp / verifyOtp.
#
# Before go-live: Supabase's built-in mailer is rate-limited and meant for
# testing. Go to Project Settings → Auth → SMTP Settings and connect your
# own provider (SendGrid, Postmark, AWS SES, etc.) so OTP emails are
# reliable and don't land in spam.

# --- AI / ML classification API (optional) ---
# If set, src/services/ai/classificationService.js will call this endpoint
# instead of the deterministic demo engine. Expected to accept a POST body of
# { description, manualCategory, imageLabel, latitude, longitude, locationName }
# and return { issueType, confidence, department }.
VITE_AI_API_URL=
VITE_AI_API_KEY=
